{"id": "EUVD-2026-76598", "enisaUuid": "57002153-7e63-32f8-a1f5-81f5c22d5008", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnfsd: fix BUG_ON in nfsd4_alloc_layout_stateid on racing delegation revoke\n\nnfsd4_alloc_layout_stateid reads fp->fi_deleg_file without holding\nfi_lock when the parent stateid is a delegation. A concurrent delegation\nrevoke via the laundromat can clear fi_deleg_file under fi_lock, causing\nnfsd_file_get() to return NULL and triggering the BUG_ON.\n\nThis race is client-reachable: two NFS clients can trigger it by having\none hold a delegation while another opens the same file to force a\nrecall. When the first client doesn't respond to the recall, the\nlaundromat revokes it. A concurrent LAYOUTGET from any client using the\ndelegation stateid hits the race window.\n\nFix this by taking fi_lock around the fi_deleg_file read in the\nSC_TYPE_DELEG path, matching the locking discipline of the\nfind_any_file() arm, and replacing the BUG_ON with a graceful error\nreturn that cleans up the partially-initialized layout stateid.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:46:07", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:48:21", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d12af460df27876661707efab3a8532146cb961f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c517f27498757e616d2a8fe6d16caad1fee422e6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/607a56fea772c1f4f4989d8e255dd4f7192d9604", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/97bda8b4284d90897a1f1922e5082ff9e35d7c7e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ca94ba36172046be6a694a7986f6931e47ed4d51"], "aliases": ["GHSA-8hmx-j653-mwq6", "CVE-2026-89686"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.66, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f51adcc-59b8-30a3-96e8-40e6dcdb4dc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "5553ee82-be24-305b-a86a-e3a0b0da4f03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c5c707f96fc9a6e5a57ca5baac892673270abe3d <ca94ba36172046be6a694a7986f6931e47ed4d51"}, {"id": "5fbfc4a0-2265-38d7-b5d1-42f5c0ce5316", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "74931dec-8650-34fd-b147-ec32c8a25dad", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c5c707f96fc9a6e5a57ca5baac892673270abe3d <c517f27498757e616d2a8fe6d16caad1fee422e6"}, {"id": "7eb40040-a0f5-38f9-ad94-bb54425a0e36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "90ea20f4-84f3-3243-80ef-a674072d8f35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c5c707f96fc9a6e5a57ca5baac892673270abe3d <97bda8b4284d90897a1f1922e5082ff9e35d7c7e"}, {"id": "96374727-6917-3c58-9194-30bdf733e034", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c5c707f96fc9a6e5a57ca5baac892673270abe3d <d12af460df27876661707efab3a8532146cb961f"}, {"id": "aadc532b-d104-324c-b1bd-aeddc4b9b311", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "c9ffe496-2e41-3923-ba9d-1bf69713e64d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.0"}, {"id": "cc967b66-b4fe-3740-91f4-1b0898a1030d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c5c707f96fc9a6e5a57ca5baac892673270abe3d <607a56fea772c1f4f4989d8e255dd4f7192d9604"}, {"id": "d81fe6c3-a0ef-39a9-986a-df39a756fc7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "da4a9b70-ee92-3fbb-be54-a3ce54ffccee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "25e59445-b055-358c-b00c-9a2716283bbf", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}